course: dictionary
lesson: 3512
title: Fatherless
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fatherless means without a father. A child can be fatherless because their father has died, has left, or is not known. «Defend the weak and the fatherless; uphold the cause of the poor and the oppressed» comes from an old book, the Psalms in the Bible, where «the fatherless» means children without fathers.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. The verse names the fatherless with the weak and the poor, and it says to «rescue the weak and the needy». So the fatherless are people who need care and protection. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Fatherless describes one fact about a family. It does not say whether a family is happy or sad. Families come in many shapes, and a fatherless child can have a loving home with a mum, grandparents, carers or other people who care for them.
fact: Fatherless means without a father.
fact: A child can be fatherless if their father has died, has left, or is not known.
fact: In old writing, «the fatherless» means children without fathers, often named with widows as people to care for.
fact: Families come in many shapes, and children without a father at home can have very happy lives.
fact: If anyone at home frightens or hurts you, tell a trusted adult, such as a teacher or family member, because your safety always comes first.
exercise: «Defend the weak and the fatherless; uphold the cause of the poor and the oppressed.» What does fatherless mean? | Living by the sea | *Without a father | Good at football | Very tall
exercise: The verse says to «rescue the weak and the needy». Which words show who needs help? | Happy and loud | Rich and proud | Tall and fast | *Weak and needy
exercise: Jamal's dad died when he was small. Which word describes Jamal's family? | *Fatherless | Ancient | Treacherous | Luminous
test: Fatherless means without a father. What does it mean? | Without a mother | *Without a father | Full of light | Very old
test: Which statement is true? | Children without a father can never be happy | A fatherless family is always sad | *Children without a father at home can have very happy lives | Only old books use the word fatherless
exam: What should a child do if they are frightened of being hurt at home? | *Tell a trusted adult, such as a teacher | Wait and hope it stops | Keep it secret forever | Hide until it is dark
